extraction_notes: "THREE THINGS THE BOOK STATES THAT THE SCHEMA DOES NOT HOLD AS NUMBERS. (1) The three W.P. Sharpshooting specialties are three instances of ONE catalog row naming three different weapons; a class grants a skill once, so the row is granted once and the three weapons are recorded in its note and in the abilities. (2) Quick-Draw Initiative scales on the P.P. ATTRIBUTE rather than on level, so it is prose, exactly as W.P. Quick Draw and W.P. Sharpshooting are stored - see docs/leveling.md on non-automatic W.P. bonuses. (3) The Horror Factor of 8 at 6th level is one the character PROJECTS; bonuses.saves.horror_factor is the save against one, so this is prose, following the demigod. The +1 extra attack with any gun and the +3 to disarm on a called shot are conditional on holding a gun and are in abilities rather than in bonuses.combat, per the reference. The book writes Basic Electronics as ''(10%)'' with no plus sign where every other entry on the list carries one; read as +10%. ''W.P. Two Modern Weapons'' and ''W.P. One Ancient Weapon'' are stored as three unrestricted W.P. picks, because the catalog does not divide the category that way. Standard Equipment stores only the catalog rows that exist; the book also lists M.D.C. body armour of choice, tinted goggles, a cowboy hat, riding and town clothes, a laser distancer, a pocket translator, a magnifying glass, a multi-optics band, a portable tool kit, a cigarette lighter, a pocket mirror, a silver cross and a wooden cross, 2-4 pairs of handcuffs, six feet of M.D.C. chain with a heavy lock, 100 ft of rope, saddlebags, a Vibro-Blade or Neuro-Mace, a six-shooter with 60-144 silver bullets, an energy or Techno-Wizard pistol, a scoped energy rifle, one more weapon of choice, 1D4+3 spare clips each, two smoke grenades, 1D4+2 flares, 1D4+4 hand grenades if the character knows demolitions, and a horse or a battered Northern Gun hovercycle at 3D4% reduced M.D.C."
