# Gunfighter

**Alignments.** The typical assassin or unscrupulous gun for hire is anarchist
or evil. Those who are honourable and live by the Code of the New West may be
any alignment, including good or selfish.

Do not confuse the Gunfighter with the Gunslinger. The Gunslinger is a
quick-draw shooter who specialises in handguns and murder - a professional
duellist and assassin. The Gunfighter is a weapons master, marksman, mechanic
where guns are concerned, and mercenary fighter: an expert in the use,
handling and repair of every type of weapon.

Most are Wild West mercenaries. Some deal or smuggle guns, some hire out as
military advisers, some become renowned heroes and lawmen, and others end as
drifters or outlaws. The book offers a comparison worth keeping: the Gunfighter
is something like a ronin, a masterless samurai - an expert in weapons, war and
fighting with no single master or cause, travelling a vast wilderness looking
for somewhere the expertise is wanted.

## Standing

Gunfighters are looked on more kindly than bounty hunters, gunslingers or even
mercenaries. Towns, ranchers, wealthy business owners and lawmen hire them as
bodyguards, bouncers, town defenders, militia leaders and deputies, and some
become sheriffs or a community''s standing champion.

Most, though, are adventurers on the prowl for action and profit, addicted to
travel and to the thrill of it. Unlike bounty hunters they are choosy about
their employers and the terms, and many will not step outside their own code
even facing death - some will turn on a dishonourable employer outright.

## Lore

Also known as the Gunman, the Vigilante, the Pistollero and the Bravo. Most
follow the Code of the New West as well as a personal code of ethics, honour
and professionalism, which is the part of the trade that harks back to the
knight and the samurai.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gunfighter');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gunfighter';

